  "debug_test_2": {
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Explain the grading system"
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "The grading system at Zakir Husain College of Engineering & Technology (ZHCET) is based on a 10-point scale. Here's a breakdown of the system:\n\n* **Letter Grades:**\n\t+ O (Outstanding): 90-100%\n\t+ E (Excellent): 80-89%\n\t+ A (Very Good): 70-79%\n\t+ B (Good): 60-69%\n\t+ C (Fair): 50-59%\n\t+ D (Pass): 40-49%\n\t+ F (Fail): Below 40%\n* **Grade Points:**\n\t+ O: 10\n\t+ E: 9\n\t+ A: 8\n\t+ B: 7\n\t+ C: 6\n\t+ D: 5\n\t+ F: 0\n* **CGPA (Cumulative Grade Point Average) Calculation:**\n\t+ The CGPA is calculated by dividing the total grade points earned by the total number of credits attempted.\n\t+ The CGPA is used to evaluate a student's overall academic performance.\n\nFor example, if a student earns the following grades in a semester:\n\n| Course | Credits | Grade | Grade Points |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Math | 3 | A | 8 |\n| Science | 4 | B | 7 |\n| English | 2 | C | 6 |\n\nThe total grade points earned would be: (3 x 8) + (4 x 7) + (2 x 6) = 24 + 28 + 12 = 64\n\nThe total credits attempted would be: 3 + 4 + 2 = 9\n\nThe CGPA would be: 64 / 9 = 7.11\n\nNote that the grading system and CGPA calculation may be subject to change, and it's always best to consult the official ZHCET website or academic regulations for the most up-to-date information."
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Explain the grading system"
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "The grading system at Zakir Husain College of Engineering & Technology (ZHCET) is based on a 10-point scale. To provide a detailed explanation, I'll break it down into the following components:\n\n### Letter Grades and Grade Points\nThe college uses the following letter grades and corresponding grade points:\n\n* **O (Outstanding)**: 90-100% - 10 grade points\n* **E (Excellent)**: 80-89% - 9 grade points\n* **A (Very Good)**: 70-79% - 8 grade points\n* **B (Good)**: 60-69% - 7 grade points\n* **C (Fair)**: 50-59% - 6 grade points\n* **D (Pass)**: 40-49% - 5 grade points\n* **F (Fail)**: Below 40% - 0 grade points\n\n### CGPA Calculation\nThe Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) is calculated by dividing the total grade points earned by the total number of credits attempted.\n\n### Example\nTo illustrate this, let's consider a student who earns the following grades in a semester:\n\n| Course | Credits | Grade | Grade Points |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Math | 3 | A | 8 |\n| Science | 4 | B | 7 |\n| English | 2 | C | 6 |\n\nThe total grade points earned would be: (3 x 8) + (4 x 7) + (2 x 6) = 24 + 28 + 12 = 64\n\nThe total credits attempted would be: 3 + 4 + 2 = 9\n\nThe CGPA would be: 64 / 9 = 7.11\n\n### Important Notes\nPlease note that the grading system and CGPA calculation may be subject to change. For the most up-to-date information, it's always best to consult the official ZHCET website or academic regulations.\n\nIf you have any further questions or would like more information on the grading system, feel free to ask."
      }
    ],
    "lastAccessed": 1775047901364
  },
